      "reasons": [
        "The definition misstates the disorder classification: the packet says anhedonia is a symptom of many psychotic disorders, with major depressive disorder and schizophrenia given as examples, but major depressive disorder is not itself a psychotic disorder.",
        "The phrase “linked to disruption in normal psychological and neurobiological functioning” is acceptable as a paraphrase, but the second sentence adds an unsupported framing of the examples as ‘several psychotic disorders’ and should not present major depressive disorder that way."
